---
// Reproduction ledger (D-080, WP1): every shipped dataset's frozen reproduction test and its result,
// pass or fail. Read from data/reproduction.json. Each frozen test file's SHA-256 is recomputed at
// build and must equal both the ledger and the package's sources.json, or the build fails.
import fs from 'node:fs';
import path from 'node:path';
import crypto from 'node:crypto';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import L from '../components/L.astro';
import Layer from '../components/Layer.astro';
import { ROOT, loadAtlas } from '../lib/atlas.mjs';
import { REPO } from '../lib/md.mjs';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const ledger = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, 'data/reproduction.json'), 'utf8'));
const atlas = loadAtlas();
const shipped = new Set(atlas.all.map((d) => d.key));
const listed = new Set(ledger.datasets.map((e) => e.package));
for (const k of shipped) if (!listed.has(k)) throw new Error(`reproduction ledger: shipped dataset ${k} has no entry`);
const rows = ledger.datasets.map((e) => {
  const dir = path.join(ROOT, 'data/packages', e.package);
  const file = path.join(dir, e.test_file);
  const actual = crypto.createHash('sha256').update(fs.readFileSync(file)).digest('hex');
  const recorded = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(dir, 'sources.json'), 'utf8')).reproduction_file?.sha256;
  if (actual !== e.sha256 || recorded !== e.sha256) throw new Error(`reproduction ledger: ${e.package} ${e.test_file} hash mismatch (file ${actual}, ledger ${e.sha256}, sources.json ${recorded})`);
  const d = atlas.all.find((x) => x.key === e.package);
  const plotted = d ? d.measurements.rows.filter((r) => !r.role || r.role === 'default').length : 0;
  const title = d?.title || e.package;
  return { ...e, d, plotted, title, name: title.split(':')[0] };
});
const kiNums = new Set(atlas.all.flatMap((d) => d.knownIssues.map((k) => k.issue)));
const issueHref = (n) => (kiNums.has(n) ? `${base}known-issues/#issue-${n}` : `${REPO}/issues/${n}`);
const nPass = rows.filter((r) => r.result === 'pass').length;
const nFail = rows.length - nPass;
const nFlag = rows.reduce((s, r) => s + (r.flagged || 0), 0);
const nRows = rows.reduce((s, r) => s + r.plotted, 0);
const label = { pass: ['Passed', 'Passed'], fail: ['Failed, on record', 'Did not fully match'] };
const mark = { pass: '✓', fail: '✕', decided: '◆', reported: '✓' };
const blob = (pkg, f) => `${REPO}/blob/main/data/packages/${pkg}/${f}`;
---
<Base title="Reproduction" active="reproduction" description="Every dataset in the Atlas, checked against what its authors published: the frozen test, its fingerprint, and the result, pass or fail.">
  <div class="doc">
    <main>
      <p class="kicker"><L t={`Reproduction · ${rows.length} datasets · ${nPass} passed · ${nFail} failed on record`} p={`Checks · ${rows.length} datasets`} /></p>
      <h1><L t="Does the Atlas reproduce what the authors published?" p="Do our numbers match the originals?" /></h1>
      <Layer as="p" class="lede"><Fragment slot="t">Before any dataset is converted, a test is written that says exactly what must match the source and how closely, and its SHA-256 fingerprint is recorded. The test is then run once and its result published. A failed test is never edited to pass: the failure stays on record, the affected measurements are flagged and ringed on every chart, and the cause is investigated in the open.</Fragment><Fragment slot="p">Before we add any data, we write down how we will check it against the original, and lock that check so it cannot be changed. Then we run it and publish what happened, even when it fails. Points that do not match are marked on every chart.</Fragment></Layer>

      <dl class="facts" style="margin:18px 0 8px">
        <div><dt><L t="Datasets" p="Datasets" /></dt><dd style="font-size:28px">{rows.length}</dd></div>
        <div><dt><L t="Tests passed" p="Matched" /></dt><dd style="font-size:28px;color:var(--ok)">{nPass}</dd></div>
        <div><dt><L t="Tests failed, on record" p="Did not fully match" /></dt><dd style="font-size:28px;color:var(--fail)">{nFail}</dd></div>
        <div><dt><L t="Flagged measurements" p="Marked points" /></dt><dd style="font-size:28px">{nFlag.toLocaleString('en-CA')} <span class="small">/ {nRows.toLocaleString('en-CA')}</span></dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="small"><L t="Fingerprints verified at build: each frozen test file's SHA-256 is recomputed when the site is built and must equal the value recorded when it was frozen. The build fails otherwise." p="Each locked check is fingerprinted, and the site will not build if any has been changed." /></p>

      <div class="tablebox" style="margin-top:18px;max-height:none" role="region" aria-label="Summary of reproduction results" tabindex="0">
        <table>
          <caption class="sr-only">Reproduction result per dataset</caption>
          <thead><tr><th class="l" scope="col">Dataset</th><th class="l" scope="col"><L t="Result" p="Result" /></th><th scope="col"><L t="Checks passed" p="Checks passed" /></th><th scope="col"><L t="Flagged" p="Marked" /></th><th class="l" scope="col"><L t="First run" p="Date" /></th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {rows.map((r) => <tr>
              <td class="l wrap"><a href={`#${r.package.replace('/', '-')}`}>{r.name}</a></td>
              <td class="l"><span class={`badge ${r.result === 'pass' ? 'ok' : 'fail'}`}><span aria-hidden="true">{mark[r.result]}</span><L t={label[r.result][0]} p={label[r.result][1]} /></span></td>
              <td>{r.checks.filter((c) => c.outcome === 'pass').length} / {r.checks.filter((c) => c.outcome === 'pass' || c.outcome === 'fail').length}</td>
              <td>{r.flagged}</td>
              <td class="l">{r.first_run}</td>
            </tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      {rows.map((r) => <section class="card" id={r.package.replace('/', '-')} style="margin-top:22px">
        <p class="cap">{r.package}</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:22px"><a href={`${base}datasets/${r.package}/`} style="color:var(--ink)">{r.title}</a></h2>
        <p style="margin:6px 0"><span class={`badge ${r.result === 'pass' ? 'ok' : 'fail'}`}><span aria-hidden="true">{mark[r.result]}</span><L t={label[r.result][0]} p={label[r.result][1]} /></span> <span class="small" style="margin-left:6px"><L t={`Frozen before ${r.frozen_before}; first run ${r.first_run}.`} p={`Locked before the data were added; run ${r.first_run}.`} /></span></p>
        <p style="margin:4px 0"><b><L t="Checked against:" p="Compared with:" /></b> <L t={r.against} p={r.against_plain} /></p>
        <ul class="checks">
          {r.checks.map((c) => <li class={c.outcome}><span class="m" aria-hidden="true">{mark[c.outcome]}</span><span><b><L t={c.name} p={c.plain} /></b><span class="sr-only"> — {c.outcome}</span>{c.outcome === 'fail' && <span class="small" style="color:var(--fail)"> (failed)</span>}{c.outcome === 'decided' && <span class="small"> (decision rule, not pass/fail)</span>}{c.outcome === 'reported' && <span class="small"> (reported, not pass/fail)</span>}<br /><span class="small"><L t={c.detail} p={c.detail} /></span></span></li>)}
        </ul>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0"><b><L t="Status:" p="Where it stands:" /></b> <L t={r.status} p={r.status_plain} /></p>
        {r.since && <p class="small" style="margin-top:6px"><b><L t="Since:" p="Since then:" /></b> <L t={r.since} p={r.since_plain} /></p>}
        <p class="small" style="margin-top:6px"><b><L t="What this establishes:" p="What this shows:" /></b> <L t={r.scope} p={r.scope_plain} /></p>
        {r.issues.length > 0 && <p class="small" style="margin-top:6px"><L t="Known issues:" p="Open problems:" /> {r.issues.map((n, k) => <>{k > 0 && ', '}<a href={issueHref(n)}>#{n}</a></>)}</p>}
        <p class="small" style="margin-top:8px;word-break:break-all"><L t="Frozen test" p="Locked check" />: <a href={blob(r.package, r.test_file)}>{r.test_file}</a> · SHA-256 <code>{r.sha256}</code> · <L t="verified at build" p="unchanged" /><br /><L t="Results" p="Results" />: {r.result_files.map((f, k) => <>{k > 0 && ' · '}<a href={blob(r.package, f)}>{f}</a></>)}</p>
      </section>)}

      <h2 id="audit" style="margin-top:36px"><L t="Independent audit" p="An outside check" /></h2>
      <Layer as="p"><Fragment slot="t">The tests above were run by the Atlas itself. An independent audit is planned and frozen (D-081, D-082): two blind readers re-derive a random 5 % of the plotted measurements (254 rows, at least 10 per dataset) from the original sources, without seeing the Atlas values, and a separate neutrality check reads the site for wording that assumes a cause. The sample is chosen by a public random beacon value published after the plan was frozen, so no one could steer it. The result will be published here, pass or fail.</Fragment><Fragment slot="p">These checks were done by us. Next, outside readers will re-check a random sample of our numbers against the original papers, without seeing ours first. The sample is picked by a public random number, so nobody can choose it. We will publish what they find.</Fragment></Layer>
      <p class="small"><a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/docs/audit/AUDIT_PLAN_v2.md`}>Audit plan (version 2)</a> · <a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/data/frozen/audit-plan-v2.json`}>its frozen hashes</a></p>
    </main>
    <aside class="toc"><p class="cap">Datasets</p>{rows.map((r) => <a href={`#${r.package.replace('/', '-')}`}>{r.name}</a>)}<a href="#audit">Independent audit</a><p class="cap" style="margin-top:14px">Related</p><a href={`${base}known-issues/`}>Known issues</a><a href={`${base}methods/`}>Methods</a></aside>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .checks { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 10px 0 0; display: grid; gap: 8px; }
  .checks li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 22px 1fr; gap: 6px; align-items: start; }
  .checks .m { font-weight: 700; text-align: center; }
  .checks li.pass .m { color: var(--ok); }
  .checks li.fail .m { color: var(--fail); }
  .checks li.decided .m, .checks li.reported .m { color: var(--muted); }
  td.wrap { white-space: normal; min-width: 12ch; }
  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; padding: 0; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
</style>
